Fix the authentication scheme sent in the MAR by ims_auth.

TS 29.229 6.3.9 defines the SIP-Auth-Data-Item scheme value "Unknown"
with a capital U; ims_auth sent "unknown". The local comparison is case
insensitive, so only the MAR changes. A strict HSS may still reject
Unknown for an IMS-AKA subscriber (TS 29.228 6.3.1 step 4).

The synchronisation MAR always used registration_default_algorithm.
TS 29.228 Table 6.3.2 allows only the IMS-AKA schemes there, so a
default of MD5 or Unknown could never resync. Use the scheme of the
challenge being resynchronised (Digest-AKAv1-MD5 or Digest-AKAv2-MD5),
falling back to Digest-AKAv1-MD5.

diff --git a/src/modules/ims_auth/authorize.c b/src/modules/ims_auth/authorize.c
index 6fa9937cb6..17c8c82845 100644
--- a/src/modules/ims_auth/authorize.c
+++ b/src/modules/ims_auth/authorize.c
@@ -132,7 +132,7 @@ str algorithm_types[] = {{"unknown", 7}, {"AKAv1-MD5", 9}, {"AKAv2-MD5", 9},
 		{"3GPP-Digest", 11}, {"TISPAN-HTTP_DIGEST_MD5", 22},
 		{"NASS-Bundled", 12}, {0, 0}};
 
-str auth_scheme_types[] = {{"unknown", 7}, {"Digest-AKAv1-MD5", 16},
+str auth_scheme_types[] = {{"Unknown", 7}, {"Digest-AKAv1-MD5", 16},
 		{"Digest-AKAv2-MD5", 16}, {"Early-IMS-Security", 18},
 		{"Digest-MD5", 10}, {"Digest", 6}, {"SIP Digest", 10},
 		{"HTTP_DIGEST_MD5", 15}, {"NASS-Bundled", 12}, {0, 0}};
@@ -693,6 +693,12 @@ int ims_resync_auth(struct sip_msg *msg, str *proute_name, str *prealm)
 			auts.len = 0;
 			auts.s = 0;
 		} else {
+			/* a resync MAR may only use an IMS-AKA scheme (TS 29.228,
+			 * Table 6.3.2): keep the scheme of the original challenge */
+			if(av->type == AUTH_AKAV1_MD5 || av->type == AUTH_AKAV2_MD5)
+				algo_type = av->type;
+			else
+				algo_type = AUTH_AKAV1_MD5;
 			if(av->is_locally_generated && ims_auth_av_mode == 1) {
 				// Locally generated AV --> do local resync
 				// auts is 14 bytes, or 112 bits --> in base64 it will be >18.(6) bytes, so 20 bytes
